{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Batch-renders multi-language VO from a structured project folder (_Raw to _Processed) with per-language overrides and CSV logging. Requires SWS and ReaImGui.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Select a track and run. Each plugin in that track's FX chain is opened in its own window, one at a time in chain order, screenshotted, and closed again. The images are saved as PNGs in Docs<Track name>\\ inside the project folder (created if needed), numbered in chain order: 01_ReaEQ.png, 02_ReaComp.png...\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires js_ReaScriptAPI (install it from ReaPack, then restart REAPER). The project must be saved first so the script knows where the project folder is.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Tips: don't move the mouse over or click on the plugin windows while it runs. If a plugin with a slow GUI comes out blank, raise WAIT_SECONDS at the top of the script.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each track = one layer. The items on that track (left to right) = that layer's variations. Select the layer items (or just the layer tracks), run the script, set options and click Build.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Default mode: builds N variations side by side, every layer aligned in each slot. Variation 1 = file 1 of every layer, variation 2 = file 2, etc. Layers with fewer files cycle (or pick randomly, if chosen). A layer with one file is reused in every variation. Combo mode: builds every possible combination of layer files.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Alignment: item start (default) or first transient per item. Optional: one region per variation, ready for Render > Project regions. Fully undoable.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires ReaImGui (install it from ReaPack).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Select any number of items (e.g. the 4+ layers of a gunshot) and run the script. Items are sorted by position and the console shows, for each layer:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab its offset from the first layer (use this as the Initial Delay in Wwise)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab its offset from the previous layer in both milliseconds and seconds, labelled with the take and track name.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Wwise's Initial Delay property is in seconds, so the "Delay (s)" column can be pasted straight in. The breakdown is also copied to the clipboard when SWS is installed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Based on "Measure distance in seconds between selected media items" by bfieser, which measured the gap between two items.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 No extensions required.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Measures LUFS and RMS for every file in the project's _Raw language folders and writes a CSV to Data. Requires SWS.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Measures LUFS, true peak and RMS of selected items without modifying the project. Prints to the console and optionally writes a CSV. Requires SWS.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Same as "Name folder items by track and number them per region", but nested folder items under a selected folder item are renamed too, each with its own folder track's name. Regular child items (media items on non-folder tracks) are still left alone, so NVK Folder Items' auto-select (which selects the children too) can stay on.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each folder item gets its folder track's name plus a counter: Footsteps_01, Footsteps_02... The counter starts again at 01 inside each region and counts left to right. Each folder track keeps its own count.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Which items: the selected items. If no items are selected, every item on the selected tracks is used. From those, every folder item (any item on a folder track, at any nesting level) is renamed. Items that aren't folder items are skipped.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Folder items with a take have the take renamed; empty ones get the item notes set, which is the text REAPER shows on an empty item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Items that don't start inside a region are left alone (change SKIP_OUTSIDE_REGIONS below to number them too). If regions overlap, the one that starts latest wins. Fully undoable.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Same as "Name items by track and number them per region", but for folder items: renames only the folder items and leaves their child items alone, so NVK Folder Items' auto-select (which selects the children too) can stay on.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each folder item gets its folder track's name plus a counter: Footsteps_01, Footsteps_02... The counter starts again at 01 inside each region and counts left to right. Each folder track keeps its own count.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Which items: the selected items. If no items are selected, every item on the selected tracks is used. From those, only folder items (any item on a folder track) are renamed. A selected item on a track under a selected folder item's track that overlaps it is treated as that folder item's child and skipped, nested folder items included. Items that aren't folder items are skipped too.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Folder items with a take have the take renamed; empty ones get the item notes set, which is the text REAPER shows on an empty item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Items that don't start inside a region are left alone (change SKIP_OUTSIDE_REGIONS below to number them too). If regions overlap, the one that starts latest wins. Fully undoable.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Renames items to their track's name plus a counter: Footsteps_01, Footsteps_02... The counter starts again at 01 inside each region and counts left to right. Each track keeps its own count, so two tracks in the same region both start at 01.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Which items: the selected items. If no items are selected, every item on the selected tracks is used.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Works on normal items (the take is renamed) and on empty items such as folder items (the item notes are set, which is the text REAPER shows on an empty item).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Items that don't start inside a region are left alone (change SKIP_OUTSIDE_REGIONS below to number them too). If regions overlap, the one that starts latest wins. Fully undoable.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Renames selected items to their region's name plus a two-digit counter (Region_01, Region_02...).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Writes a text list of every plugin REAPER knows about, grouped by format, to the resource folder and opens it. Requires REAPER 6.37+.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Combs through every script registered in the Action List (all sections: Main, MIDI Editor, Media Explorer...) and finds the ones whose script file no longer exists on disk. Shows them in a list so you can pick which to remove, backs up reaper-kb.ini first, then unregisters them.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Without ReaImGui it falls back to a simple Yes/No prompt that removes all missing scripts at once.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Wwise Tool\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Send audio from REAPER straight into Wwise. Built with Lua and ReaImGui.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Source: the selected items, just the selected folder items (child items ignored, for NVK Folder Items' auto-select), or whatever REAPER's render settings produce (regions, stems, region matrix...).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Import destination: type a Wwise path or grab the Wwise selection.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Hierarchy mapping: build Wwise containers above each Sound (Actor-Mixers, Random/Sequence/Switch/Blend Containers, Virtual Folders, Work Units) named with REAPER wildcards like $region, $track, $item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Property templates per level, Sound SFX or Sound Voice (with language), Originals subfolder (wildcards allowed).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Tabs, each a whole setup you can flick between. Conflict handling, structure and settings presets, export/import of the whole configuration, live preview (new vs existing objects), transfer summary. One Wwise undo step per transfer.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Auto mono/stereo: a Sound whose left and right match is made mono (also for folder items). Click the preview's Channels column to force Mono or Stereo for a Sound or a whole container, or drag/Shift/Ctrl+click to set many rows at once.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Streaming: turn on Stream per Sound or container from the preview's Streaming column, or automatically for Sounds longer than a set length.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Loop: set Sounds to loop (infinite) from the preview's Loop column.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fast: untouched WAV items import without rendering; edited items render in one pass; everything is imported in one Wwise call.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 "Wwise Tool - Quick send" sends the selected items with the window's last settings, without opening the window. Give it a shortcut.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Needs ReaImGui (ReaPack > ReaTeam Extensions) and Wwise with WAAPI on: Wwise > Project > User Preferences > Enable Wwise Authoring API (HTTP port 8090).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Full guide: https://github.com/jaysabins/reascripts/blob/main/Wwise/jsabins_Wwise%20Tool_README.md\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Not affiliated with or endorsed by Audiokinetic. Wwise is a trademark of Audiokinetic Inc.\par}
}
